Subject: [PATCH] build: Aequera vendor, profile, and user agent identity

Why Firefox source must change:
  application.ini's Vendor and Profile decide where profiles live
  (%APPDATA%\<Vendor>\<Profile>) and, in compiled builds, the vendor half
  of the registry keys, launcher, background tasks, and default-browser
  agent identity. Firefox declares both as project flags: only the
  project's moz.configure may imply them; a mozconfig is refused. Left as
  "Mozilla", an Aequera build shares a vendor tree with Firefox.
  The user agent's product token comes from MOZ_APP_UA_NAME, falling back
  to the application name: unset, every request says "Aequera/<version>"
  and no "Firefox/" token, which sites treat as an unknown browser
  (captchas, degraded pages) and which singles Aequera users out. Also a
  project flag.

What it changes:
  - MOZ_APP_VENDOR "Mozilla" -> "Aequera".
  - MOZ_APP_PROFILE "Aequera" (profile root %APPDATA%\Aequera\Profiles).
  - MOZ_APP_UA_NAME "Firefox": the user agent is Firefox's own.
  - MOZ_APP_ID stays Firefox's, keeping WebExtension compatibility.
  Everything else of the product identity is supported configuration:
  tools/build/mozconfig.branding (branding directory, basename, remoting
  name). Artifact builds run Mozilla's prebuilt binary, where this flag
  has no effect; their launch ini carries UAName=Firefox instead
  (tools/build/aequera_app_ini.py).

Depends on: nothing.
Validation: generated dist/bin/application.ini carries Vendor=Aequera,
  Profile=Aequera; navigator.userAgent ends in "Firefox/<version>"; the
  Aequera shell gate and Firefox's sidebar, tab, and bookmarks suites.
Upstream risk: low; three literal values next to MOZ_APP_ID.

diff --git a/browser/moz.configure b/browser/moz.configure
index 446e8637d053..2091af8ed9a5 100644
--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -11,7 +11,15 @@ imply_option("MOZ_NORMANDY", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_PROFILE_MIGRATOR", True)


-imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Mozilla")
+# Aequera: application.ini Vendor and Profile, i.e. the profile root
+# (%APPDATA%\Aequera\Profiles) and the vendor half of the Windows registry
+# and launcher identity. Only the project may imply these (not a mozconfig).
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Aequera")
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_PROFILE", "Aequera")
+# Aequera: the user agent names Firefox, not the application name
+# (Aequera), so sites see an ordinary Firefox: web compatibility, and no
+# rarer fingerprint than any other Firefox. Also a project flag.
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_UA_NAME", "Firefox")
 imply_option("MOZ_APP_ID", "{ec8030f7-c20a-464f-9b0e-13a3a9e97384}")
 # Include the DevTools client, not just the server (which is the default)
 imply_option("MOZ_DEVTOOLS", "all")
